HYPOTHESIS EVALUATION
========================================================================================================================

H1 (Periodicity prior gap):
  Best PCR (pcr_alpha1.0): 51.7139 vs Baseline: 57.6813 (delta=-5.9674)
  SUPPORTED: PCR reduces test RMSE by 5.9674

H2 (In-training contrastive provides regularization):
  PCR best overfitting gap: 14.6037
  Baseline overfitting gap: 26.9833
  SUPPORTED: PCR reduces overfitting

H3 (GIN sufficient per Small-Graph Paradox):
  GIN with 5 layers, hidden_dim=256, mean_pool: 407,556 params
  Baseline test RMSE: 57.6813
  (Reference: Day 1 GIN Trimer was 50.19 with 3 layers)

Domain-specific vs generic augmentation:
  PCR (monomer-trimer pairs): 51.7139
  Random (edge masking): 55.4380
  Domain-specific positive pairs are better by 3.7241

Data augmentation vs contrastive:
  GRIN (augmentation only): 54.8395
  PCR (augmentation + contrastive): 51.7139
  Contrastive adds value beyond data augmentation
